<title>SWEDEN: P&amp;U gets nod in Sweden for Nicorette tablets.</title>
<headline>P&amp;U gets nod in Sweden for Nicorette tablets.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish/U.S. drugs company Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn said on Wednesday that Sweden's drug authorities had approved the company's Nicorette tablets that are used to help people give up smoking.</p>
<p>P&amp;U said in a statement that Nicorette tablets would be launched in Sweden in the second half of 1997 and would be sold over-the-counter, prescription free.</p>
<p>P&amp;U said Nicorette products are also available in the form of chewing gum, plaster, inhaler and nasal spray.</p>
</text>
